; Zone: 0.16.172.in-addr.arpa
; Type: Reverse / Master
; Managed via: Synology DNS Server UI (http://10.0.1.15:5010)
; Serial: 2026052201
;
; SCOPE: 172.16.0.0/24 — first /24 of the VPN / WireGuard peer range.
; The ACL in named.conf.additions covers 172.16.0.0/12, but this zone file only
; handles 172.16.0.x. If peers are in 172.16.1.x or beyond, create an additional
; /24 reverse zone in the Synology UI (domain "1.16.172") and add a matching zone
; block in named.conf.additions.
;
; Zone name in Synology UI: enter "0.16.172" (UI appends .in-addr.arpa automatically).
; Synology stores the zone file as: 0.16.172.in-addr.arpa
;
; This zone does NOT cover the NAS LAN IP (10.0.1.15) —
; LAN reverse lookups are in 1.0.10.in-addr.arpa (10.0.1.rev.zone).
;
; PTR host field = last octet only (it is a /24 zone):
;   172.16.0.2  →  host field: 2
;   172.16.0.15 →  host field: 15
;
; Neighboring /24 zones to create as peers expand beyond 172.16.0.x:
;   1.16.172.in-addr.arpa  →  covers 172.16.1.x
;   2.16.172.in-addr.arpa  →  covers 172.16.2.x

$TTL 7200
$ORIGIN 0.16.172.in-addr.arpa.

@   IN  SOA  otsorundscore.olutechsys.com. admin.olutechsys.com. (
              2026052201
              3600
              900
              604800
              300 )

@           IN  NS   otsorundscore.olutechsys.com.

; Add PTRs as WireGuard/VPN peers get fixed assignments in 172.16.0.x:
; 2           IN  PTR  peer2.olutechsys.com.
